    "faq_section": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How is this different from regular forearm trainers?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Generic forearm tools use simple spring resistance that doesn’t replicate the actual arm-wrestling motion. This trainer uses a <strong>hydraulic resistance system</strong> engineered to match the exact pulling angle and tension curve of a real match. Your strength transfers directly to performance.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Can beginners use this trainer?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely. With <strong>12 resistance levels</strong> ranging from light rehab work to competition-grade intensity, this trainer is designed for everyone — from complete beginners to seasoned arm wrestlers. Start at level 1-3 and progress at your own pace.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Do I need a training partner?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>No. That’s one of the biggest advantages. Set it on any flat surface, adjust the resistance, and pull. You get targeted, consistent reps on your own schedule — whether it’s 6am before work or 11pm after the gym. No partner, no gym, no setup.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How often should I use it?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Consistency is key. We recommend <strong>3-4 sessions per week</strong> of 15-20 minutes each. Most users report noticeable forearm and grip strength gains within <strong>2-3 weeks</strong> of consistent training.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Does it require assembly or mounting?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Zero assembly required. The trainer comes ready to use out of the box. Just place it on any flat surface — desk, table, counter, or workbench. No suction cups, no mounting hardware, no drilling. Ready in seconds.</p>",
